# Chat request

The one door to a model: an OpenAI-shaped chat-completions request through
OpenRouter, paid for from the contributor's own key. Building it is pure; the
call is made by `host_tools.lg`, the only place the key is read, and the key goes
into one request header and nowhere else.

## Note
One message — `system`, `user` or `assistant` — and what is asked of a model;
`temperatureBp` is the temperature in basis points (2,000 is 0.2).

## A ChatMessage has:
    a role, which is Text.
    a content, which is Text.

## A ChatRequest has:
    a model, which is Text.
    a messages, which is Seq of ChatMessage.
    a maxTokens, which is Int.
    a temperatureBp, which is Int.

## Note
Where requests and the price list (which needs no key) are.

## To chatCompletionsUrl () -> Text:
    Return "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions".

## To modelsUrl () -> Text:
    Return "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models".

## Note
The headers: the key as a bearer token, and OpenRouter's two attribution headers.

## To openRouterHeaders (apiKey: Text) -> Map of Text to Text:
    Let mutable h be a new Map of Text to Text.
    Set h at "Authorization" to "Bearer " + apiKey.
    Set h at "Content-Type" to "application/json".
    Set h at "HTTP-Referer" to "https://macsad.com".
    Set h at "X-Title" to "MaCSad factory".
    Return h.

## Note
Basis points as the exact JSON decimal they stand for: `2000` is `0.2`.

## To bpDecimal (bp: Int) -> Json:
    If bp % 10000 is equal to 0:
        Return a new JNum with n (bp / 10000).
    Let mutable m be bp.
    Let mutable sc be 0 - 4.
    While m % 10 is equal to 0:
        Set m to m / 10.
        Set sc to sc + 1.
    Return a new JDec with mant m and scale sc.

## Note
The request body, in a fixed order and canonical form, so the prompt hash over it
is the same on every machine. `usage.include` asks for the call's cost.

## To chatRequestJson (r: ChatRequest) -> Text:
    Let mutable msgs be a new Seq of Json.
    Repeat for m in r's messages:
        Push (a new JObj with entries [a new JEntry with key "role" and val (a new JStr with s m's role), a new JEntry with key "content" and val (a new JStr with s m's content)]) to msgs.
    Let usage be a new JObj with entries [a new JEntry with key "include" and val (a new JBool with b true)].
    Let head be [a new JEntry with key "model" and val (a new JStr with s r's model), a new JEntry with key "messages" and val (a new JArr with elems msgs)].
    Let tail be [a new JEntry with key "max_tokens" and val (a new JNum with n r's maxTokens), a new JEntry with key "temperature" and val bpDecimal(r's temperatureBp)].
    Return jsonSerialize(a new JObj with entries (head + tail + [a new JEntry with key "usage" and val usage])).

## Note
The prompt hash: the SHA-256 of the exact body. Two calls with one hash asked one
model one thing, which is what replay recordings are keyed by.

## To promptSha (r: ChatRequest) -> Text:
    Return bytesToHex(sha256(text_bytes(chatRequestJson(r)))).

## Note
A request for the tests.

## To sampleRequest () -> ChatRequest:
    Let system be a new ChatMessage with role "system" and content "You write LOGOS kernel proofs.".
    Return a new ChatRequest with model "openai/gpt-4o-mini" and messages [system, a new ChatMessage with role "user" and content "Prove goal."] and maxTokens 1000 and temperatureBp 2000.

## Test: a request body is canonical JSON in a fixed order

Let body be "{{\"model\":\"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\"messages\":[{{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You write LOGOS kernel proofs.\"}},{{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Prove goal.\"}}],".
Expect that chatRequestJson(sampleRequest()) is equal to body + "\"max_tokens\":1000,\"temperature\":0.2,\"usage\":{{\"include\":true}}}}".

## Test: temperatures are exact decimals and the key stays in its header

Expect that jsonSerialize(bpDecimal(15)) is equal to "0.0015".
Expect that jsonSerialize(bpDecimal(12500)) is equal to "1.25".
Expect that item "Authorization" of openRouterHeaders("sk-or-test") is equal to "Bearer sk-or-test".
Expect that chatRequestJson(sampleRequest()) contains "sk-or" is equal to false.

## Test: a different temperature is a different prompt

For all booleans hotter:
    Let mutable r be sampleRequest().
    If hotter:
        Set r's temperatureBp to 9000.
    Expect that (promptSha(r) is equal to promptSha(sampleRequest())) is equal to (not hotter).
